}
}  PF11 (the Right key) moves the fields right of JOBNAME, PF10 (the Left
}  key) moves them back. Further right are:
}
{  ASID     }The address space id.
{  EXCP-CNT }The I/O (EXCPs) of the address space so far.
{  CPU-TIME }The processor time of the current step, in seconds.
{  SR       }Why it was swapped out: TI, TO terminal input or output
}            wait, LW long wait, XS auxiliary storage shortage, RS real
}            storage shortage, DW detected wait, RQ requested, NQ enqueue
}            exchange, EX exchange, US unilateral.
{  DMN      }The domain.
}
}  The ? command, typed alone on the command line, puts the fields into
}  another order: ASID, EXCP-CNT and CPU-TIME first, then REAL, PAGING,
}  SIO, CPU%, DP, POS, SR, PGN and DMN. ? again gives the first order.
}
}
}
}
}
